<h1 id="preface">Preface</h1>

<p>Recently I happened to look at AVKit and found a lot of new content inside. Among it is a UI control called <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">AVRoutePickerView</code>, which I planned to study. Actually it’s very common — you can see it in the system Control Center by swiping down the screen, when you connect headphones or wireless Bluetooth devices.</p>

<p><img src="/assets/images/20190417AVRoutePickerView/RouteChange2.avif" alt="Route Change" /></p>

<p>Here’s a real-world example in NetEase Cloud Music:</p>

<p><img src="/assets/images/20190417AVRoutePickerView/RouteChange1.avif" alt="Route Change" /></p>

<p>This control is mainly used for AirPlay casting and audio route switching.</p>

<p>So today I’ll learn about this new control with everyone.</p>

